n with a walrus moustache - DPLA - 142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b (page 1)","license":"Public domain","creator":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_man_with_a_walrus_moustache_-_DPLA_-_142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b_(page_1).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/A_man_with_a_walrus_moustache_-_DPLA_-_142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b_%28page_2%29.jpg/960px-A_man_with_a_walrus_moustache_-_DPLA_-_142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b_%28page_2%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","full":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f2/A_man_with_a_walrus_moustache_-_DPLA_-_142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b_%28page_2%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","title":"A man with a walrus moustache - DPLA - 142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b (page 2)","license":"Public domain","creator":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_man_with_a_walrus_moustache_-_DPLA_-_142073069112b7c5452ab55bb3563f8b_(page_2).jpg","source":"Wikimedia Commons"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/12d9fa1b-dc71-4799-ac42-1751e7e0b07d/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/2118/1641610496_37c168de6f_b.jpg","title":"'walrus moustache man'","license":"BY-NC-ND 2.0","creator":"steve loya","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/65669043@N00/1641610496","source":"Flickr"},{"url":"https://api.openverse.org/v1/images/d86c1bc4-6ac9-49ba-8525-f2192e48808f/thumb/","full":"https://live.staticflickr.com/52/163400691_f830370c64_b.jpg","title":"Walrus moustache","license":"BY-NC 2.0","creator":"Max Sparber","page":"https://www.flickr.com/photos/11828135@N00/163400691","source":"Flickr"}],"links":{"studies":[],"trials":[],"label":null,"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Meat Eaters vs. Vegetarians","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/meat-eaters-vs-vegetarians/286897","site":"T Nation · 1 posts · 2020"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Walrus moustache — Grokipedia","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Walrus_moustache"},{"title":"Walrus moustache - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walrus_moustache"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Jawline & face shape","chain":["Grow upper-lip hair long and untrimmed over the mouth","Adds bulk and covers the upper lip","Rugged, mature, character-heavy face"],"effect":"direct","text":"A walrus moustache changes the face's upper-lip area by covering it with dense hair. People wear it for a bold, vintage or rugged look."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Walrus_moustache","lead":["The walrus moustache has thick, bushy whiskers that drop over the mouth, like the whiskers of a walrus [1][2].","It adds hair mass over the upper lip, which wearers use to look older, more rugged or more distinguished. It was very popular among scientists, philosophers and politicians in the late 19th and early 20th centuries, fell out of favour in the 1920s, and had a brief revival during the 1960s counterculture [1]."],"infobox":[["Type","Moustache style"],["Peak popularity","Late 19th to early 20th century [1]"],["Notable wearers","Mark Twain, Nietzsche, Theodore Roosevelt, Sam Elliott [1][2]"],["Related styles","Handlebar, chevron, horseshoe [2]"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Whiskers are thick and bushy and hang over the mouth; in some versions the hair extends down the cheeks to join sideburns [1]. Compared with the handlebar, which is waxed into upward curls, the walrus relies on natural droop [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Wikipedia describes the style as present in Celtic and Gaulish men and strongly present in Polish Sarmatian culture, where it symbolised patriotism and nobility from the 16th to 20th century [1]. Wearers include King John III Sobieski, Otto von Bismarck, Nietzsche, Mark Twain, Theodore Roosevelt, John Lennon, Wilford Brimley, Sam Elliott and Jamie Hyneman [1]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Biology","paras":["Grokipedia attributes moustache thickness to androgen-driven conversion of vellus hair to terminal hair around the upper lip, with density influenced by genetics [2]."],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1500s-1900s","event":"Symbol of Polish Sarmatian identity [1]"},{"year":"Late 1800s","event":"Peak popularity [1]"},{"year":"1920s","event":"Decline [1]"},{"year":"1960s","event":"Brief revival [1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Walrus moustache","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walrus_moustache","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Walrus moustache","url":"https://grokipedia.com/page/Walrus_moustache","source":"Grokipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Meat Eaters vs. Vegetarians","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/meat-eaters-vs-vegetarians/286897","site":"T Nation · 1 posts · 2020"}]}